---
import { count, recognizedNotModeled, supported } from '../data/extensions';
---

<p>
  The library models <strong>{count}</strong> extension names. The reader branches on the {
    supported.length
  } listed below; every other name inside a format's accepted set is recorded as a no-op toggle, so
  a format spec naming one parses rather than aborting. A toggle naming anything outside a format's
  accepted set is rejected.
</p>

<h4>Supported</h4>
<p class="tokens">
  {supported.map((name) => <code>{name}</code>)}
</p>

<h4>Recognized, behavior not yet modeled</h4>
<p>
  These names have an enum variant, so a format spec may toggle them and the toggle is recorded, but
  the reader does not yet branch on the construct:
</p>
<p class="tokens">
  {recognizedNotModeled.map((name) => <code>{name}</code>)}
</p>

<style>
  .tokens {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.35rem;
  }
</style>
